{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>But He saves from the sword</b> — the needy, that is, from the sword of enemies." "<b>From their mouth</b> — for if they hunger, an enemy could besiege them. And the matter here: when He desires to discipline mankind — He withholds rain in its season, and when they turn back to Him — He answers them and saves them."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Resolved an unspecified referent: the comment clarifies that 'from the sword' means 'from the sword of enemies,' with 'the needy' understood as the object of rescue."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:50.880862917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}